''Germanic cognates:'' Old Frisian {{term|bar|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|bar|lang=osx}}, Middle Dutch {{term|bar|lang=dum}}, {{term|baer|lang=dum}} (Dutch {{term|bar|lang=nl}}, {{term|baar|lang=nl}}), Old High German {{term|bar|lang=goh}} (German {{term|bar|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|berr|lang=non}} (Swedish {{term|bar|lang=sv}}, Norwegian Nynorsk {{term|berr|lang=nn}}).

''Indo-European cognates:''  Balto-Slavic {{m|ine-bsl-pro|*basas}} (Lithuanian {{m|lt|bãsas}}, Latvian {{term|bass|lang=lv}}, Russian {{term|босой|tr=bosój|lang=ru}}, Polish {{term|bosy|lang=pl}}), Albanian {{term|mbath||I wear|lang=sq}}.

